{"term":"sketch","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:55c99c10ff7e581ca1","definition":"To make a brief, basic drawing.","example":"I usually sketch with a pen rather than a pencil.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive","register":"ambitransitive","wordFamily":["resketch","sketchability","sketchable","sketch out","unsketched"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sketch#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fb76dcf36f5c0e3407","definition":"To describe briefly and with very few details.","example":"He sketched the accident, sticking to the facts as they had happened.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["resketch","sketchability","sketchable","sketch out","unsketched"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sketch#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ae41cad4438701ae6d","definition":"A rapidly executed freehand drawing that is not intended as a finished work, often consisting of a multitude of overlapping lines.","example":"Orion hit a rabbit once; but though sore wounded it got to the bury, and, struggling in, the arrow caught the side of the hole and was drawn out.[…]. Ikey the blacksmith had forged us a spearhead after a sketch from a picture of a Greek warrior; and a rake-handle served as a shaft.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["resketch","sketchability","sketchable","sketch out","unsketched","biosketch","composite sketch","foresketch","police sketch","sketch-ass","sketchbook","sketcher","sketchist","sketchlike","sketchmaster","sketch pad","sketchwriter","sketchy","thumb-sketch","word sketch"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sketch#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e499d3b481e13a4ab0","definition":"A rough design, plan, or draft, as a rough draft of a book.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["croquis"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["resketch","sketchability","sketchable","sketch out","unsketched","biosketch","composite sketch","foresketch","police sketch","sketch-ass","sketchbook","sketcher","sketchist","sketchlike","sketchmaster","sketch pad","sketchwriter","sketchy","thumb-sketch","word sketch"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sketch#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:74326fd72b9055ca8e","definition":"A brief description of a person or account of an incident; a general presentation or outline.","example":"I have to write a character sketch for a novel study.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["pen picture","pen portrait"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["resketch","sketchability","sketchable","sketch out","unsketched","biosketch","composite sketch","foresketch","police sketch","sketch-ass","sketchbook","sketcher","sketchist","sketchlike","sketchmaster","sketch pad","sketchwriter","sketchy","thumb-sketch","word sketch"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sketch#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8f8197a9fdbef9a2b4","definition":"A brief, light, or unfinished dramatic, musical, or literary work or idea; especially a short, often humorous or satirical scene or play, frequently as part of a revue or variety show.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["skit"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["resketch","sketchability","sketchable","sketch out","unsketched","biosketch","composite sketch","foresketch","police sketch","sketch-ass","sketchbook","sketcher","sketchist","sketchlike","sketchmaster","sketch pad","sketchwriter","sketchy","thumb-sketch","word sketch"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sketch#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:79fa4a2cfb07b40652","definition":"An amusing person.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"informal","register":"informal","wordFamily":["resketch","sketchability","sketchable","sketch out","unsketched","biosketch","composite sketch","foresketch","police sketch","sketch-ass","sketchbook","sketcher","sketchist","sketchlike","sketchmaster","sketch pad","sketchwriter","sketchy","thumb-sketch","word sketch"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sketch#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:518a7647b7a931acf9","definition":"A lookout; vigilant watch for something.","example":"to keep sketch","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Ireland, slang","register":"Ireland, slang","wordFamily":["resketch","sketchability","sketchable","sketch out","unsketched","biosketch","composite sketch","foresketch","police sketch","sketch-ass","sketchbook","sketcher","sketchist","sketchlike","sketchmaster","sketch pad","sketchwriter","sketchy","thumb-sketch","word sketch"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sketch#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:033edcf086eb71625f","definition":"A humorous newspaper article summarizing political events, making heavy use of metaphor, paraphrase and caricature.","example":"A very capable journalist, he wrote the Parliamentary sketch for the Pall Mall and the Westminster Gazette for several years.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK","register":"UK","wordFamily":["resketch","sketchability","sketchable","sketch out","unsketched","biosketch","composite sketch","foresketch","police sketch","sketch-ass","sketchbook","sketcher","sketchist","sketchlike","sketchmaster","sketch pad","sketchwriter","sketchy","thumb-sketch","word sketch"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sketch#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:35da28f44b793c8a17","definition":"A formal specification of a mathematical structure or a data type described in terms of a graph and diagrams (and cones (and cocones)) on it. It can be implemented by means of “models”, which are functors which are graph homomorphisms from the formal specification to categories such that the diagrams become commutative, the cones become limiting (i.e., products), the cocones become colimiting (i.e., sums).","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["resketch","sketchability","sketchable","sketch out","unsketched","biosketch","composite sketch","foresketch","police sketch","sketch-ass","sketchbook","sketcher","sketchist","sketchlike","sketchmaster","sketch pad","sketchwriter","sketchy","thumb-sketch","word sketch"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sketch#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:53cfe5a0e921d95285","definition":"Sketchy, shady, questionable.","example":"You call at 9 am on a Saturday, lucky I'm even awake. [...] Then expect me to pick you up at a gas station near a loony bin, that's sketch. I don't even want to ask what you're doing.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"informal","register":"informal","wordFamily":["resketch","sketchability","sketchabl